First of all this is a messy mapping and we will have to make some shortcuts.

Fir FHIR examples check:
https://nhsconnect.github.io/Dose-Syntax-Implementation/dosage-doseQuantity-freq-period.html
================================================

Example 1:

  {
  "timing": {
    "repeat": {
      "frequency": 3,
       "period": 1,  //  must be 1 if unit is daily, since we map daily doses only here due to daily dosage mapping, important here is we state that also in the code, only daily is supported for now.
      "periodUnit": "d",  // allow only day, minute, hour, second (and below no week or smt, since this has to go to !!!!non_dailyCluster)
      "timeOfDay": [
        "08:00:00"
      ]
    }
  },
  "doseQuantity": {
    "value": 600,
    "unit": "mg",
    "system": "http://unitsofmeasure.org",
    "code": "mg"
  },
  "rateRatio": {
    "numerator": {
      "value": 600,
      "unit": "mg",
      "system": "http://unitsofmeasure.org",
      "code": "mg"
    },
    "denominator": {// basically this means from 08:00:00 - 11:00:00 but we dont add that but for understanding
      "value": 1,
      "unit": "h",
      "system": "http://unitsofmeasure.org",
      "code": "h"
    }
  }
}

Dosage
 [openEHR-EHR-COMPOSITION.report.v1]/content[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1]/description[at0017]/items[openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.dosage.v2]/items[at0144] = 600 mg // dosage quantity

Administration rate
 [openEHR-EHR-COMPOSITION.report.v1]/content[openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1]/description[at0017]/items[openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.dosage.v2]/items[at0134] = 600mg/h  // numerator/denominator

